  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>The number of elements in sets&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;be five and two respectively,</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now Cartesian product will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Number of subsets having three elements&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Number of subsets having four&nbsp;elements<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></p><p>Number of subsets having five&nbsp;elements&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math></p><p>Number of subsets having six&nbsp;elements&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math></p><p>So, number of subsets having atleast&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and at most&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;elements will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>210</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>252</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>210</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>792</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
